  "findings": [
    "Five of six repeats have a dominant native post-startup renderer task; every overlapping V8 sample is program except one idle sample. It is not an attributed application JavaScript function.",
    "Concurrent compositor/GPU-process wall waits with small thread CPU strongly implicate rendering/presentation synchronization in this SwiftShader lab; exact native operation and behavior on real GPU remain unverified.",
    "First scene render takes 271\u2013475 ms. CPU samples map the dominant named first-use work to Three.js WebGLProgram.onFirstUse; PMREM generation takes 43\u201371 ms.",
    "Targeted experiment: async shader precompile and coalesced initial paints, retaining model/materials/resolution/animation."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Phase marks and V8 CPU sampling add diagnostic overhead; these scores are not final uninstrumented acceptance.",
    "All durations under phaseMeasures/rawTask are unscaled raw wall time; simulated TBT and thread CPU are separate timing domains.",
    "No field INP or real-GPU performance closure."
  ],
  "candidateExperiment": {
    "status": "prepared-not-measured",
    "changes": [
      "Await public WebGLRenderer.compileAsync after full scene/light/environment setup before first render.",
      "Coalesce fit/resume/intersection notifications through one requestAnimationFrame; avoid repeating setSize/setPixelRatio for unchanged dimensions."
    ],
    "preserved": [
      "geometry",
      "materials",
      "lighting",
      "DPR caps",
      "30 fps cadence",
      "3D animation and controls"
    ],
    "lifecycle": "Ordinary pending unmount detaches listeners/canvas and defers destructive GPU disposal until compilation settles.",
    "knownLibraryLimitation": "Three.js 0.160 compileAsync has no cancellation API. External WebGL context loss during its internal completion polling may prevent its promise from settling; app callbacks/listeners/animation are stopped immediately, but termination of the library poll is not guaranteed. No private internals, monkeypatches or fake timeout cancellation were introduced."
  }
